      neighborhoodName: 'Bergenline Avenue',
      insight: `Bergenline Avenue in West New York functions as a dense commercial spine with mixed-use buildings that have flat roofs over ground-floor storefronts and multiple residential floors above. The repair needs here center on flat membrane maintenance, parapet flashing that deteriorates from the thermal cycling amplified by the Palisades elevation, and drain systems that clog with debris from the commercial activity below. While Bergenline shares its name with the Union City section to the south, the West New York portion sits at a higher elevation where wind reaches the rooftops with greater force, meaning that membrane seam separations and parapet failures happen more frequently here than on the identical building types just blocks to the south across the municipal boundary.`,
