      neighborhoodName: '60th Street Area',
      insight: `The 60th Street area contains a cluster of row houses and smaller multi-family buildings with pitched roofs featuring complex geometries including dormers, valleys, and hip configurations. The repair challenges here combine the wind factor common to all of West New York with the water concentration issues that complex rooflines create. Valley flashing failures are the most frequent repair we perform in this neighborhood, because the wind-driven rain loads at this elevation push more water into valleys than the original flashing installations were designed to handle. We see valley overflow during heavy rain events where water bypasses the flashing channel entirely, running under shingle courses and into the building envelope where it causes interior damage that is often misdiagnosed as a plumbing leak by property owners.`,
