      insight: `Park Avenue residential blocks feature walk-up apartment buildings of four to six stories with flat roofs that are typical of mid-century West New York construction. The repair challenges here involve aging membrane systems that have been patched multiple times over the decades, combined with limited staging access on the narrow residential streets. The proximity to James J. Braddock Park means that mature trees in the park drop debris onto nearby roofs, clogging drains and creating organic matter buildup that accelerates membrane deterioration. Our repairs in the Park Avenue area frequently include drain clearing and debris management as part of the scope because addressing the membrane damage without resolving the debris accumulation guarantees a repeat failure within a season.`,
